WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.419
Final Review and Graduation.

2
00:00:02.699 --> 00:00:06.689
Day 94 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Career phase.

3
00:00:08.439 --> 00:00:09.463
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:11.172
You made it to the last day!

5
00:00:11.452 --> 00:00:17.639
Today you'll test yourself across all five phases, see how far you've come, and plan what to practise next.

6
00:00:17.919 --> 00:00:20.969
Do the self-test without looking back at the lessons first.

7
00:00:22.319 --> 00:00:23.173
Part 1.

8
00:00:23.453 --> 00:00:24.327
Part 1:

9
00:00:24.607 --> 00:00:26.378
English basics (Phase 1).

10
00:00:27.628 --> 00:00:39.425
Make questions for the answers: ? then I've worked here for six years. ? then The train leaves from platform 4. ? then No, I didn't get the email. ? then It costs 1,200 rupees.

11
00:00:39.705 --> 00:00:40.921
Fix the mistakes:

12
00:00:41.201 --> 00:00:45.191
Myself Ravi, I am working in Infosys since 2019.

13
00:00:46.541 --> 00:00:48.205
Did you went to office yesterday?

14
00:00:48.485 --> 00:00:50.639
Please do the needful and revert back.

15
00:00:50.919 --> 00:00:52.925
If it will rain, we cancel the trip.

16
00:00:54.275 --> 00:00:55.192
Success:

17
00:00:55.472 --> 00:00:56.325
Answers.

18
00:00:56.605 --> 00:00:58.141
How long have you worked here?

19
00:00:58.421 --> 00:00:59.125
2.

20
00:00:59.405 --> 00:01:01.517
Which platform does the train leave from?

21
00:01:01.797 --> 00:01:02.544
3.

22
00:01:02.824 --> 00:01:04.104
Did you get my email?

23
00:01:04.384 --> 00:01:05.685
How much does it cost?

24
00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:06.733
5.

25
00:01:07.013 --> 00:01:07.867
I'm Ravi.

26
00:01:08.147 --> 00:01:11.347
I've been working at Infosys since 2019.

27
00:01:11.627 --> 00:01:13.483
Did you go to the office yesterday?

28
00:01:13.763 --> 00:01:14.509
7.

29
00:01:14.789 --> 00:01:17.093
Could you please specific action and reply?

30
00:01:17.373 --> 00:01:19.336
If it rains, we'll cancel the trip.

31
00:01:20.686 --> 00:01:21.561
Part 2.

32
00:01:21.841 --> 00:01:22.715
Part 2:

33
00:01:22.995 --> 00:01:24.745
Communication (Phase 2).

34
00:01:25.995 --> 00:01:27.552
Rewrite with the point first:

35
00:01:27.832 --> 00:01:33.720
So I was checking logs and then I saw the cache was empty and then... so the release will be one day late.

36
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.155
Write two clarifying questions for:

37
00:01:36.435 --> 00:01:37.821
Make the dashboard better.

38
00:01:38.101 --> 00:01:39.317
Replace the filler:

39
00:01:39.597 --> 00:01:43.267
Basically, actually, I think maybe we could, like, try caching.

40
00:01:44.617 --> 00:01:45.534
Success:

41
00:01:45.814 --> 00:01:46.966
Sample answers.

42
00:01:47.246 --> 00:01:48.974
The release will be one day late.

43
00:01:49.254 --> 00:01:52.177
The cache was empty, so we need to re-run the tests.

44
00:01:52.457 --> 00:01:58.537
Which part of the dashboard matters most to you? / What does 'better' mean: faster, clearer, or more data?

45
00:01:58.817 --> 00:02:00.417
I suggest we try caching.

46
00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:02.663
Part 3.

47
00:02:02.943 --> 00:02:03.817
Part 3:

48
00:02:04.097 --> 00:02:06.380
Everyday conversations (Phase 3).

49
00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:10.809
Say each of these out loud in one or two sentences:

50
00:02:11.089 --> 00:02:14.353
At a railway counter, ask for a ticket and which platform.

51
00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:18.067
Tell a doctor about a symptom: where, what kind, since when.

52
00:02:18.347 --> 00:02:20.779
Complain politely to a neighbour about noise.

53
00:02:21.059 --> 00:02:24.750
Report a missing item in a food delivery, with your order ID.

54
00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:28.785
Call an ambulance: what happened, exact location, landmark.

55
00:02:29.065 --> 00:02:32.201
Tell a gym trainer your goal and one health limitation.

56
00:02:33.551 --> 00:02:37.092
Ask a landlord about deposit, notice period and repairs.

57
00:02:38.442 --> 00:02:39.359
Success:

58
00:02:39.639 --> 00:02:40.791
Sample answers.

59
00:02:41.071 --> 00:02:44.527
One ticket to Mysuru on the 6:15 train, please.

60
00:02:44.807 --> 00:02:46.450
Which platform does it leave from?

61
00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:49.503
I've had a sharp pain in my lower back for three days.

62
00:02:49.783 --> 00:02:51.106
It's worse in the morning.

63
00:02:51.386 --> 00:02:53.050
Hi, sorry to bother you.

64
00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:56.061
The music is quite loud in our flat after 11.

65
00:02:56.341 --> 00:02:58.047
Could you turn it down a little at night?

66
00:02:58.327 --> 00:03:03.319
My order 48213 arrived without the paneer biryani.

67
00:03:03.599 --> 00:03:05.050
Could you refund it, please?

68
00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:11.367
A man has collapsed and isn't breathing properly, at 12 MG Road, opposite the Metro station.

69
00:03:11.647 --> 00:03:13.098
Please send an ambulance.

70
00:03:14.448 --> 00:03:16.091
I want to lose eight kilos.

71
00:03:16.371 --> 00:03:20.339
I have some lower back pain, so I need to avoid heavy lifting at first.

72
00:03:20.619 --> 00:03:23.712
How much is the deposit, and is it fully refundable?

73
00:03:23.992 --> 00:03:26.851
What's the notice period, and who pays for repairs?

74
00:03:28.201 --> 00:03:29.118
Part 4.

75
00:03:29.398 --> 00:03:30.614
Part 4 and 5:

76
00:03:30.894 --> 00:03:33.582
Workplace and career (Phases 4 to 5).

77
00:03:34.832 --> 00:03:37.392
Give a 3-line stand-up update with a blocker.

78
00:03:37.672 --> 00:03:41.277
Raise a risk to your manager with two options and a recommendation.

79
00:03:41.557 --> 00:03:46.187
Explain a technical issue to a non-technical person with one analogy.

80
00:03:46.467 --> 00:03:49.603
Say no to extra work politely, with an alternative.

81
00:03:49.883 --> 00:03:52.677
Answer Tell me about yourself in under 60 seconds.

82
00:03:52.957 --> 00:03:56.221
Respond to a salary offer that's lower than you expected.

83
00:03:57.571 --> 00:03:58.211
Tip:

84
00:03:58.491 --> 00:03:59.537
Score yourself.

85
00:03:59.817 --> 00:04:06.131
For each item, give yourself 2 (easy, confident), 1 (I could do it, slowly) or 0 (I got stuck).

86
00:04:06.411 --> 00:04:08.011
40 plus is excellent.

87
00:04:08.291 --> 00:04:12.025
25 to 39: re-do the days where you scored 0.

88
00:04:12.305 --> 00:04:16.614
Under 25: repeat Phase 1 and the everyday days you'll need soonest.

89
00:04:16.894 --> 00:04:18.707
There's no shame in a second round.

90
00:04:20.057 --> 00:04:21.017
Part 5.

91
00:04:21.297 --> 00:04:22.385
Before and after.

92
00:04:23.635 --> 00:04:28.137
Redo the self-assessment and compare with the plan you made in the previous lesson.

93
00:04:28.417 --> 00:04:29.377
Write down:

94
00:04:29.657 --> 00:04:32.537
3 situations that used to scare me and don't now.

95
00:04:32.817 --> 00:04:34.374
3 mistakes I've fixed.

96
00:04:34.654 --> 00:04:36.681
3 things I still want to improve.

97
00:04:38.031 --> 00:04:38.969
Part 6.

98
00:04:39.249 --> 00:04:40.593
What to practise next.

99
00:04:41.843 --> 00:04:42.910
Second round:

100
00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:47.777
Go through the course again, faster: one day = role-play + quiz only.

101
00:04:48.057 --> 00:04:49.849
You'll notice how much easier it is.

102
00:04:50.129 --> 00:04:51.323
New situations:

103
00:04:51.603 --> 00:04:55.657
Use the conversation generator for any topic the course doesn't cover.

104
00:04:55.937 --> 00:04:56.939
Real people:

105
00:04:57.219 --> 00:05:00.761
Join a meetup, Toastmasters club or English-speaking group.

106
00:05:01.041 --> 00:05:03.003
Speak once a week in front of others.

107
00:05:03.283 --> 00:05:04.265
Daily habit:

108
00:05:04.545 --> 00:05:07.809
Keep using the Phrase Bank and the Daily Practice Checklist.

109
00:05:09.159 --> 00:05:10.076
Success:

110
00:05:10.356 --> 00:05:11.615
Congratulations!.

111
00:05:11.895 --> 00:05:14.412
Every day of practice is a real achievement.

112
00:05:14.692 --> 00:05:18.361
Confidence comes from repetition, and you've done the repetitions.

113
00:05:18.641 --> 00:05:20.092
Keep speaking every day.

114
00:05:21.442 --> 00:05:22.381
Part 7.

115
00:05:22.661 --> 00:05:25.925
Practice conversation: telling your manager what you learned.

116
00:05:27.175 --> 00:05:29.201
Here is how the conversation goes.

117
00:05:29.481 --> 00:05:32.063
You seem much more confident in meetings lately.

118
00:05:32.343 --> 00:05:33.452
What changed?

119
00:05:33.732 --> 00:05:34.649
Thank you!

120
00:05:34.929 --> 00:05:41.159
I followed a 75-day communication course: one lesson a day, with role-plays.

121
00:05:41.439 --> 00:05:42.783
What helped the most?

122
00:05:43.063 --> 00:05:48.865
Putting the main point first, and practising real conversations out loud before they happened.

123
00:05:50.215 --> 00:05:51.815
The conversation continues.

124
00:05:52.095 --> 00:05:52.970
It shows.

125
00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:56.194
Would you be open to sharing a few tips with the new joiners?

126
00:05:56.474 --> 00:05:57.669
I'd love to.

127
00:05:57.949 --> 00:06:00.445
Maybe a 30-minute session next month?

128
00:06:00.725 --> 00:06:01.770
Perfect.

129
00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:03.735
Let's put it in the calendar.

130
00:06:05.085 --> 00:06:06.621
That's the end of this lesson.

131
00:06:06.901 --> 00:06:11.552
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

132
00:06:11.832 --> 00:06:17.955
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

